<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Revenue attribution</h2>
<p>Revenue Attribution readiness starts with provable consent records and instant post-checkout suppression across each app running revenue attribution sends. For revenue attribution, a promo arriving after a purchase, refund, or open support case burns trust faster than weak revenue attribution creative ever could.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>No revenue attribution promos without proof; transactional messages only</td><td>Every revenue attribution send stands on documented consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Lead revenue attribution newcomers with teaching and social proof</td><td>Revenue Attribution margin suffers when discounts arrive first</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Revenue Attribution reminder with product context; discount withheld</td><td>Revenue Attribution high-intent window deserves margin discipline</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Pause revenue attribution promos; switch to post-purchase teaching</td><td>Post-checkout revenue attribution pitches trigger regret and opt-outs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Freeze revenue attribution promos until refund or return closes</td><td>Open revenue attribution cases reset what the shopper tolerates</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Remove chronic revenue attribution non-openers pre-complaint</td><td>Shields revenue attribution sender reputation and inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Revenue Attribution SMS obeys quiet hours and caps</td><td>Revenue Attribution SMS complaints cost more per incident</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Revenue Attribution B2B routing stays account-specific</td><td>B2B revenue attribution mis-sends risk contract breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Gate revenue attribution journeys behind address verification</td><td>Low-grade revenue attribution signups drag deliverability</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Revenue Attribution QA profiles excluded from reporting</td><td>Revenue Attribution test sends skew attribution reads</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Revenue Attribution exceptions stay undocumented-free</td><td>Ad-hoc revenue attribution exceptions break traceability</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Reconfirm revenue attribution consent where timestamps are missing</td><td>Timestamp-less revenue attribution consent is legal exposure</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Revenue attribution</h2>
<p>Attributed revenue is not profit for revenue attribution. A self-funding revenue attribution program survives a full cost model: subscription, contact or send overages, SMS credits, capture tooling, templates, agency time, and every point of revenue attribution discount margin. For revenue attribution, a stack at fifteen percent of attributed margin needs simplification first, optimization second.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. For revenue attribution, free plans always bind somewhere; identify whether contacts, sends, branching, or support caps your revenue attribution motion first.</p>
